{"type":"message","id":"4d05ed2c","parentId":"2bbb5445","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:20:53.352Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — I checked, and the reason is pretty clear:\n\nThe Google Drive draft was generated from `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md`, but the feature image never got inserted into that file because the embed check used `-f /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` on a **symlink**. In bash, `-f` returns false for that symlink path in this flow, so the pipeline took the fallback branch:\n\n- it printed: **`[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.`**\n- then it copied `/tmp/crypto-article.md` as-is\n- so the DOCX uploaded to Drive had **no feature image at the top**\n\nMeanwhile, the actual image file did exist and was valid:\n- `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` → symlink to `/tmp/crypto-run-20260520-074303/feature.jpg`\n- real image size: **1,076,796 bytes**\n\nSo this was not an image-generation failure — it was an **image embedding check bug during the Drive export step**.\n\nIn short:  \n**Drive draft missed the image because the export step incorrectly decided the image file wasn’t valid, even though the real file existed.**\n\nIf you want, I can fix that pipeline check so future Drive drafts always include the feature image."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2161,"output":268,"cacheRead":27520,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29949,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779265247711,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhWScUTBjTRlHPnxvZ57p6jHiOXgj"}}
{"type":"message","id":"1632e350","parentId":"4d05ed2c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:27:17.516Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:5691449303\",\n  \"message_id\": \"535\",\n  \"reply_to_id\": \"534\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"sender\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-20 08:27 UTC\",\n  \"has_reply_context\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Sawan bhardwaj (5691449303)\",\n  \"id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"name\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"username\": \"hero_fr_fun\"\n}\n```\n\nReplied message (untrusted, for context):\n```json\n{\n  \"sender_label\": \"seo_agent_openclaw_bot\",\n  \"body\": \"Yes — I checked, and the reason is pretty clear:\\n\\nThe Google Drive draft was generated from /tmp/crypto-with-image.md, but the feature image never got inserted into that file because the embed check used -f /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg on a symlink. In bash, -f returns false for that symlink path in this flow, so the pipeline took the fallback branch:\\n\\n• it printed: [IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.\\n• then it copied /tmp/crypto-article.md as-is\\n• so the DOCX uploaded to Drive had no feature image at the top\\n\\nMeanwhile, the actual image file did exist and was valid:\\n\\n• /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg → symlink to /tmp/crypto-run-20260520-074303/feature.jpg\\n• real image size: 1,076,796 bytes\\n\\nSo this was not an image-generation failure — it was an image embedding check bug during the Drive export step.\\n\\nIn short:\\nDrive draft missed the image because the export step incorrectly decided the image file wasn’t valid, even though the real file existed.\\n\\nIf you want, I can fix that pipeline check so future Drive drafts always include the feature image.\"\n}\n```\n\nbut wp publisher have this image which was generated only drive is missing so I need the culprit for this to fix you don't do anythgin any changes just answer here without doing nay changes anywhere"}],"timestamp":1779265637514}}
{"type":"message","id":"4bab8d5f","parentId":"1632e350","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:27:51.676Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — exactly. The **culprit is not the WP publisher**.\n\n### Why WordPress has the image\nThe WP publisher works differently:\n- it takes `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` directly\n- uploads it to WordPress\n- sets it as the featured image there\n\nSo WordPress can still have the image even if the Drive doc missed it.\n\n### Why Google Drive missed the image\nThe Drive version depends on this **Step 4 preprocessing block**:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg ] && [ $(stat -c%s /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg 2>/dev/null || echo 0) -gt 10000 ]; then\n    printf '![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\n\\n' | cat - /tmp/crypto-article.md > /tmp/crypto-with-image.md\n    echo \"[IMAGE] Embedded valid feature image.\"\nelse\n    cp /tmp/crypto-article.md /tmp/crypto-with-image.md\n    echo \"[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.\"\nfi\n```\n\nThat block is the **actual culprit**.\n\n### Proof\nYou already have the smoking gun:\n- the export log said: **`[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.`**\n- and `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` started directly with `META`, not with:\n  `![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)`\n\nThat means the image was dropped **before pandoc** ever made the DOCX.\n\nSo the failure chain is:\n\n1. creator generated the image successfully ✅  \n2. wp-publisher used that image directly ✅  \n3. Drive export step incorrectly decided the image was “not valid” ❌  \n4. `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` was created without the image ❌  \n5. pandoc converted that image-less markdown into DOCX ❌  \n6. Drive upload faithfully uploaded the image-less DOCX ❌\n\n### Bottom line\nThe thing to fix is:\n\n**the Drive export image-embed check in Step 4**, not the creator, not the WP publisher, and not the Drive uploader.\n\nIf you want the shortest possible diagnosis to keep in mind:\n\n> **WP uses the JPEG directly; Drive only gets whatever Step 4 embeds into markdown first. Step 4 skipped the embed, so Drive never had a chance to include the image.**"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":620,"output":1519,"cacheRead":29824,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":31963,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779265637517,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhWYyWp7ISr5396QKWRf5wWmELOFK"}}
