{"type":"message","id":"2e21f122","parentId":"28787dc3","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:37:44.193Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell them the **test proved the image existed, but the Drive export step skipped embedding it**.\n\nYou can say it like this:\n\n> I tested the pipeline output and confirmed the feature image was generated successfully and existed at `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`. But during the Google Drive export path, the preprocessing step logged **“No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.”**  \n> That means the DOCX was created **without** the feature image before upload.  \n> So the issue is in the **Drive export embed check**, not in image generation and not in the WordPress publisher.\n\nIf you want an even shorter version:\n\n> The test shows the image file was valid, but the Drive export step failed its embed check and skipped inserting it into the markdown/DOCX. That’s why WordPress had the image and Drive did not.\n\nIf they ask for the exact evidence, give them these two points:\n\n- image file existed and was valid: `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` → real file size `1076796` bytes  \n- export log said: **`[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.`**\n\nThat’s the cleanest “what the test proved” answer."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1998,"output":247,"cacheRead":31104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33349,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779266258555,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhWivoL9LvIAq6jRWKKA9DqmTYgcA"}}
