{"type":"message","id":"6344779c","parentId":"f9d7ec39","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:41:30.316Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — I continued the chain and completed the Drive retest.\n\n### What the retest proved\n- Creator reran successfully\n- Feature image validated: **1,038,367 bytes**\n- Export step now logged: **`[IMAGE] Embedded valid feature image (1038367 bytes).`**\n- The rebuilt markdown starts with the image line:\n  `![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-run-20260520-074303/feature.jpg)`\n\nSo this retest confirms the issue was in the **Drive export embed step**, and when that step embeds correctly, the Drive draft is rebuilt with the image included.\n\n### Fresh Drive draft link\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1KVpaZYZNgPubGgqG2u9mUMiHmUsxPWtv/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=109667066179998081561&rtpof=true&sd=true\n\n### What to tell them\nYou can now say:\n\n> I reran the chain from creator through Drive export. The test confirmed the feature image was generated correctly, and when the export step embedded it properly, the new Google Drive draft was created with the image included.  \n> So the culprit is the Drive export image-embedding step, not the creator and not the WordPress publisher.\n\nIf you want, I can help you phrase that as a tight one-line message for them."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":342,"output":292,"cacheRead":38144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38778,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779266484364,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhWmYiOHcZ5fuSM0W78zDrj5QaPjl"}}
{"type":"message","id":"3b52d881","parentId":"6344779c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:42:08.907Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"System (untrusted): [2026-05-20 08:41:24 UTC] Exec completed (kind-nud, code 0) :: { \"file\": { \"id\": \"1KVpaZYZNgPubGgqG2u9mUMiHmUsxPWtv\", \"mimeType\": \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\", \"name\": \"Crypto News - 2026-05-20 RET…\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:5691449303\",\n  \"message_id\": \"550\",\n  \"reply_to_id\": \"549\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"sender\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-20 08:42 UTC\",\n  \"has_reply_context\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Sawan bhardwaj (5691449303)\",\n  \"id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"name\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"username\": \"hero_fr_fun\"\n}\n```\n\nReplied message (untrusted, for context):\n```json\n{\n  \"sender_label\": \"seo_agent_openclaw_bot\",\n  \"body\": \"Done — I continued the chain and completed the Drive retest.\\n\\nWhat the retest proved\\n\\n• Creator reran successfully\\n• Feature image validated: 1,038,367 bytes\\n• Export step now logged: [IMAGE] Embedded valid feature image (1038367 bytes).\\n• The rebuilt markdown starts with the image line:\\n![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-run-20260520-074303/feature.jpg)\\n\\nSo this retest confirms the issue was in the Drive export embed step, and when that step embeds correctly, the Drive draft is rebuilt with the image included.\\n\\nFresh Drive draft link\\n\\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1KVpaZYZNgPubGgqG2u9mUMiHmUsxPWtv/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=109667066179998081561&rtpof=true&sd=true\\n\\nWhat to tell them\\n\\nYou can now say:\\n\\nI reran the chain from creator through Drive export. The test confirmed the feature image was generated correctly, and when the export step embedded it properly, the new Google Drive draft was created